Problem Statement
Development and testing servers were running 24/7, leading to unnecessary AWS costs during non-working hours.
Solution
Implemented an automated scheduling mechanism to shut down non-production EC2 instances outside business hours and restart them automatically when required.


Before Implementation
Instances Running:
24 Hours/Day

Monthly Runtime:
720 Hours/Month
After Implementation
Instances Running:
10 Hours/Day

Monthly Runtime:
~220 Hours/Month
Savings
Runtime Reduction:
~70%

Monthly Cost Savings:
Significant reduction depending on instance type and count.
Business Impact
Reduced unnecessary AWS spending.
Eliminated manual start/stop operations.
Improved operational efficiency.
Enabled standardized infrastructure governance.
Increased visibility through CloudWatch monitoring.
